    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "On February 4, 2021, Yearn Finance’s v1 yDAI vault on Ethereum lost $11 million after an attacker repeatedly manipulated Curve 3pool’s stablecoin balances, exploiting loose slippage limits and permissionless strategy calls to drain vault funds through a flash-loan-powered cycle. The v1 yDAI vault’s Curve strategy accounted for deposits and withdrawals using spot exchange rates from Curve 3pool, which were manipulable within a single transaction. Loose slippage checks (1%), disabled withdrawal fees (0%), and permissionless access to push deposits enabled the attacker to profitably cycle pool imbalances, draining value from the vault. The system assumed…"
